    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="5" relname="span">One way to help avoid poor web designs is to head them off before they even get created.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="7" relname="concession">Although the functionality doesn't generally exist now,</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="7" relname="span">how effective do you think it would be to incorporate guidelines &amp; suggestions into popular personal web design products like FrontPage?</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="elaboration">For some of the problems people have listed above (like scrolling to the right), you could even use the development tool to prevent that web page from behaving in a poor manner!</segment>
        <group id="5" type="span"/>
        <group id="6" type="span" parent="1" relname="means"/>
        <group id="7" type="span" parent="6" relname="span"/>
    </body>
